<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Azad Kashmir Travel Guide - Royal Route Travel & Tours</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"> <!-- Apni CSS file ka link yahan rakhein -->
</head>
<body>

    <header class="guide-header">
        <h1>Complete Azad Kashmir Travel Guide</h1>
        <p>Discover Neelum Valley, Majestic Waterfalls, and High-Altitude Lakes</p>
    </header>

    <main class="guide-container">
        
        <!-- Hero / Intro Image -->
        <section class="guide-hero">
            <img src="public/guides/kashmir/Neelam Valley.jpg" alt="Neelum Valley Kashmir">
        </section>

        <!-- Intro Text -->
        <section class="guide-section">
            <h2>Overview of Azad Kashmir</h2>
            <p>Known as Heaven on Earth, Azad Kashmir offers lush green valleys, roaring rivers, cascading waterfalls, and serene alpine lakes. Whether you are seeking adventure or relaxation, Neelum Valley is the heart of Kashmir tourism.</p>
        </section>

        <!-- Top Attractions -->
        <section class="guide-section">
            <h2>Must-Visit Attractions in Kashmir</h2>

            <!-- Neelum River -->
            <div class="spot-card">
                <img src="public/guides/kashmir/Neelam-River.jpg" alt="Neelum River">
                <h3>1. Neelum River</h3>
                <p>The lifeline of Neelum Valley, flowing parallel to the main road with stunning lush green mountain views on both sides.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Dhani Waterfall -->
            <div class="spot-card">
                <img src="public/guides/kashmir/dhani waterfall.jpg" alt="Dhani Waterfall">
                <h3>2. Dhani Waterfall</h3>
                <p>Located near Muzaffarabad, Dhani Waterfall is a famous tourist stop known for its roaring water during late spring and summer months.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Kundal Shahi Waterfall -->
            <div class="spot-card">
                <img src="public/guides/kashmir/Kundalshahi Waterfall.jpg" alt="Kundalshahi Waterfall">
                <h3>3. Kundal Shahi Waterfall</h3>
                <p>A roaring stream of crystal-clear water flowing into the Neelum River, making it a soothing resting spot for travelers.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Arang Kel -->
            <div class="spot-card">
                <img src="public/guides/kashmir/Arangkel.jpg" alt="Arang Kel">
                <h3>4. Arang Kel</h3>
                <p>Accessible via a scenic cable car ride from Kel followed by a short trek, Arang Kel is a lush green hilltop village offering breathtaking views.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Ratti Gali Lake -->
            <div class="spot-card">
                <img src="public/guides/kashmir/ratti gali lake.jfif" alt="Ratti Gali Lake">
                <h3>5. Ratti Gali Lake</h3>
                <p>An alpine glacial lake located at 12,130 feet. Known for its turquoise water surrounded by vibrant wildflowers during summer.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Ratti Gali in Winter -->
            <div class="spot-card">
                <img src="public/guides/kashmir/Ratti Gali in winter.jfif" alt="Ratti Gali in Winter">
                <h3>Ratti Gali Lake in Winter</h3>
                <p>During winter months, the lake transforms into a completely frozen wonderland blanketed in snow, ideal for thrill-seekers.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Taobatt -->
            <div class="spot-card">
                <img src="public/guides/kashmir/Taobatt.jpg" alt="Taobatt">
                <h3>6. Taobatt</h3>
                <p>The last point of Neelum Valley bordering the Line of Control. Famous for its thick green pastures, wooden houses, and serene nature.</p>
            </div>

        </section>

        <!-- Travel Tips -->
        <section class="guide-section">
            <h2>Best Time to Visit & Travel Tips</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Best Season:</strong> May to October for green lush views and accessible lakes.</li>
                <li><strong>Transport:</strong> 4x4 Jeeps are recommended for routes heading to Ratti Gali Lake and Taobatt.</li>
                <li><strong>Identity Documents:</strong> Always carry original CNIC/Passports for security checkpoints along the route.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

    </main>

</body>
</html>
